"ej.murshe":"I am an osek murshe — I reclaim VAT",
"ej.murshe.hint":"<b>Murshe</b> deducts input VAT by the category shares — the journal shows what comes back in the VAT report.<br><b>Patur</b> gets no VAT back: the full receipt amount goes into recognized expenses by the category share. The checkbox switches the whole journal.",
"ej.note":"The journal is a planning estimate, not bookkeeping. Keep original documents for 7 years.",
"ej.rules.b":"<p><b>100% for both tax and VAT:</b> office rent/coworking, materials and goods, software, accountant and lawyer, bank fees, professional books and refresher courses, professional insurance.</p><p><b>Car</b> — 45% for tax, ⅔ of VAT on running costs (fuel, service, insurance). <b>Mobile phone</b> — about 50% for tax (annual cap applies), ⅔ VAT. <b>Home office</b> — by the share of the work room (we assume 25%): arnona, electricity, vaad bayit, internet; VAT on a residential flat is not deducted — a grey zone.</p><p><b>Kibud</b> (office coffee and snacks) — 80%, no VAT. <b>Client gifts</b> — up to 240 ₪ per person per year (log who and what for). <b>Representative clothing</b> — 80%, VAT only with a business logo. <b>Restaurants and meals (esh״l)</b> — not recognized at all.</p><p>Keep receipts and invoices for 7 years. The shares are planning guidance; edge cases are your accountant's call.</p>",
"ej.rules.t":"What counts and how much (verified 08.2026)",
