"f101.btn":"Build my cheat sheet",
"f101.h":"📋 Form 101 cheat sheet",
"f101.hint":"Form 101 is filled at hiring and every January. A wrong checkbox = overpaying tax all year. Below are the general filling rules; your status, children and aliyah month are taken from your profile.",
"f101.i.base":"Section א׳ — personal details exactly as in your document: teudat zehut (תעודת זהות) or passport (דרכון), your actual address, marital status. Further sections cover spouse, children, other income, a tax-coordination request and the signature — fill them per your situation, going by the headings (section numbering differs between form years).",
"f101.i.extra":"Your additional grounds (+{n} points: degree, alimony, discharge, etc.) — tick them on Form 101 and attach certificates; for a degree or professional diploma file Form 119 (טופס 119) with a diploma copy.",
"f101.i.foreign":"B1 / 2(a)5: Form 101 is filled too — by passport (darkon, דרכון). Do NOT tick «toshav Israel»; credit points are usually 0 (2.25 for B1 caregivers).",
"f101.i.kids":"Children ({n}): fill the children table with birth dates — the age-based points come from it. For a child with a disability attach the certificate (NII disabled-child allowance or Form 116א).",
"f101.i.oleh":"Oleh chadash (עולה חדש): tick the new-immigrant item and attach the teudat oleh (תעודת עולה) — you are in month {m} of the 54 benefit months.",
"f101.i.resident":"Tick «toshav Israel» (תושב ישראל — Israeli tax resident) — without it even the basic credit points are not applied.",
"f101.i.second":"Several employers: with the main one tick «this is my main job», with the second tick «I have other income» and file a tiyum mas (תיאום מס — tax coordination), otherwise the second salary is taxed at the maximum rate.",
"f101.i.when":"When: at every new job and every January. If you do not file it, the employer must withhold tax at the maximum rate.",
"f101.note":"A push reminder will arrive in early January (if notifications are on).",
"inc.cash.warn":"⚠️ If this payment is in cash, mind the cash law: the limit is 6,000 ₪ per deal with a business (fine 15–30%). Transfers, checks and cards have no limit.",
