"zr.turn":"Turnover {y} (income journal)",
"zr.who.b":"<p><b>Conditions (all at once):</b> annual turnover up to the osek patur ceiling (~122,833 ₪ in 2026); you work personally, no employees; income is from your own work, not passive (rent, dividends — no).</p><p><b>What changes:</b> 30% of turnover is recognized automatically instead of real expenses — no receipts needed for tax (still keep them for yourself). Real expenses can no longer be deducted: the route is chosen per year and marked in the annual reporting.</p><p><b>Note:</b> the rules are new (2024 reform) and the effect on personal deductions (pension, hishtalmut) depends on your case — check with an accountant before switching.</p>",
"zr.who.t":"Who qualifies for osek zair and how to switch",
"acc.shimua.body":"<p><b>What it is:</b> a shimua is a hearing where you must be allowed to speak BEFORE a dismissal decision. The duty comes not from statute but from labour-court case law (the Guterman precedent) — and it applies to every employer, at any tenure, and also to major changes of terms: cutting hours, transfer, relocation.</p><p><b>Before the hearing — check the invitation:</b><br>☐ written and in advance — reasonable time to prepare (days, not hours);<br>☐ with SPECIFIC reasons (events, dates, facts), not «you are not a fit»;<br>☐ date, place and participants stated;<br>☐ ask in advance for the documents the employer relies on;<br>☐ you may bring a lawyer or a union representative.</p><p><b>At the hearing:</b><br>☐ a protocol is kept — demand a copy;<br>☐ answer every claim with your version (prepare written notes);<br>☐ the decision must NOT be announced on the spot: a ready dismissal letter at the end of the meeting marks a sham procedure.</p><p><b>After:</b> an answer within a reasonable time, in writing and reasoned, showing your arguments were considered (per the National Labour Court, 01.2026). Dismissal by phone call or text without a procedure is a gross violation.</p><p><b>If there was no shimua or it was a formality:</b> the labour court can cancel the dismissal or award compensation ON TOP of severance and notice — at the court’s discretion, in practice roughly 1 to 12 monthly salaries. Keep everything: the invitation, the protocol, the dismissal letter, the dates. A Zoom shimua is acceptable when justified and fully by the rules; in person is preferred.</p>",
"acc.shimua.t":"🗣 Pre-dismissal hearing (shimua): checklist",
"acc.pension.body":"<p><b>The rates on your payslip.</b> The mandatory minimum: 6% from your salary + 6.5% employer (tagmulim) + 6% employer to severance (pitzuim) — 18.5% in total, unchanged since 2017. Cleaning and construction have higher rates — see the industry guide.</p><p><b>What section 14 is.</b> By default severance pay comes at dismissal: a monthly salary per year of service. Section 14 of the Severance Pay Law changes the scheme: the employer deposits pitzuim into your fund every month — and that money becomes yours.</p><p><b>Open the payslip and check the pitzuim percentage:</b><br>• <b>8.33%</b> — section 14 applies in full: on dismissal the employer tops up nothing, it is all in the fund;<br>• <b>6%</b> — only part is covered (about 72%): on dismissal with severance rights the employer MUST pay the difference (hashlamat pitzuim). Claim it in your final settlement.</p><p><b>The key upside of s.14:</b> the accumulated pitzuim are yours even if you resign, whatever the reason (except deprivation by court for grave misconduct).</p><p><b>YOU choose the fund, not the employer</b> (s.20 of the Provident Funds Law): keren pensia, kupat gemel or bituach menahalim — any on the market. A fund cannot be imposed on you, even if it is written into the contract.</p><p><b>No choice — you go to a default fund.</b> These are 4 selected funds (Altshuler Shaham, Meitav, More, Infinity; the tender runs to 31.10.2028) with fees far below the cap: 1% of deposits and 0.22% of savings — against the maximum of 6% and 0.5%. Anyone can join, no medical questionnaire, they cannot refuse. Compare with your own dmei nihul — the default fund often beats an old personal one.</p><p><b>How to check your savings:</b><br>• free: Har HaKesef — itur.mof.gov.il, shows forgotten and inactive accounts;<br>• the full picture of all accounts including hishtalmut: the pension clearing house (hamislaka hapensionit), up to ~20 ₪ per request;<br>• match the payslip amounts against the fund statement — missing or late transfers are a violation.</p>",
"acc.pension.t":"🏦 Pension: section 14 and choosing your fund",
