"gl.h":"📖 Payslip glossary: what every line means",
"gl.hint":"Open your payslip next to this and go line by line.",
"gl.gross.t":"Gross (שכר יסוד / ברוטו)",
"gl.gross.b":"Pay BEFORE deductions: base + extras (overtime, bonuses, travel). Tax and contributions are computed from it. Check it against your contract.",
"gl.tax.t":"Income tax (מס הכנסה)",
"gl.tax.b":"Progressive 10–50% minus credit points. On low salaries it's often ₪0 after the points — that's normal.",
"gl.bl.t":"National Insurance + health (ביטוח לאומי / דמי בריאות)",
"gl.bl.b":"Social security and health tax: reduced rate up to ₪7,703, full above. Foreign workers have different (lower) rates and no health tax.",
"gl.pens.t":"Pension / tagmulim (תגמולים)",
"gl.pens.b":"Your 6% + employer's 6.5% into a pension fund. Mandatory after 6 months (or day one with an active fund — retroactive from month 3). No line after half a year — a violation.",
"gl.pitz.t":"Severance (פיצויים)",
"gl.pitz.b":"Severance accruing with the employer or in the fund: 8.33% = §14 in full (nothing to add on dismissal), 6% — the employer owes the difference on dismissal.",
"gl.hish.t":"Hishtalmut fund (קרן השתלמות)",
"gl.hish.b":"Savings fund: your 2.5% + employer's 7.5%. Mandatory in cleaning, security (from the general minimum), construction per sector rules. Tax-free withdrawal after 6 years.",
"gl.ot.t":"Overtime (שעות נוספות)",
"gl.ot.b":"First 2 hours over the day's norm — 125%, then 150%. Must be a separate line with the hour count. “Included in the salary” with no hour tracking is illegal.",
"gl.nes.t":"Travel (נסיעות)",
"gl.nes.b":"Commute pay: mandatory up to ₪22.60/day for days actually worked, unless the employer provides transport or you live within 500 m.",
"gl.hav.t":"Havra'a (דמי הבראה)",
"gl.hav.b":"“Recuperation pay”: after a year of tenure, 5–10 days a year by seniority × day rate (private sector ~₪418). Paid yearly in summer or monthly.",
"gl.hag.t":"Holiday pay (דמי חגים)",
"gl.hag.b":"Holiday pay for hourly workers after 3 months — unless you skipped the day before/after without permission. Working ON a holiday — separate line at 150%.",
"gl.zvira.t":"Balances: vacation & sick (צבירת חופשה / מחלה)",
"gl.zvira.b":"Vacation and sick-day balances: vacation accrues from 12 days/yr, sick — 1.5 days/mo (up to 90). Balances must grow if unused. Compare with “My balance” in the Timesheet.",
"gl.pts.t":"Credit points (נקודות זיכוי)",
"gl.pts.b":"Personal tax discounts: 2.25 base (men) / 2.75 (women) + children, aliyah, degree. One point = ₪242/mo less tax. Check the number on the payslip — mistakes are common.",
"gl.tium.t":"Tax coordination (תיאום מס)",
"gl.tium.b":"Mark of coordinated tax across two jobs. Second job with no tium — 47% withheld from it. Details in the refund card above.",
"rep.h":"📅 Reporting calendar",
"rep.hint":"Key dates of the year for employees, the self-employed and accountants.",
"ret.chk":"Working pensioner",
"ret.hint":"<b>What it is.</b> Retirement age in Israel: men — 67, women — 62–65. If you keep working as an employee past it, your National Insurance and health-tax deductions are lower than usual or absent altogether; income tax and the tax credit points (nekudot zikuy) stay regular.<br><b>Turn it on or not?</b> Turn it on if you have already reached retirement age. Not yet — leave it off.<br><b>Good to know.</b> The old-age pension itself (kitzbat zikna) is not subject to income tax.",
"ret.kitzba":"Do you receive the old-age pension (kitzbat zikna) from Bituach Leumi?",
"ret.age":"Age",
"ret.newjob":"Hired here after 67 and receiving a pension (not an NII benefit)",
"ret.newjob.hint":"<b>What it is.</b> The employer must make pension contributions for working pensioners unless all three conditions are met at once:<br>1. You joined your current job aged 67+.<br>2. You left your previous job aged 67+.<br>3. You already receive an occupational/savings pension (Bituach Leumi benefits do not count).<br><b>Tick it or not?</b><br>Tick: if you were hired after 67, left the previous job after 67 and already receive pension payments.<br>Do not tick: if you keep working at the same place, left the previous job before 67, or have not started drawing a pension yet.<br><b>Good to know.</b> Even when the employer is legally exempt, they are fully entitled to contribute voluntarily by agreement.",
"ret.pens.note":"With your settings the employer may be legally exempt from pension deposits (hired after 67 + left the previous job at 67+ + a pension not from Bituach Leumi): missing pension lines on the payslip are not a violation by themselves. Deposits being made anyway is fine too. Unsure — check the conditions on kolzchut.org.il.",
"ret.inctest":"Before age 70 kitzbat zikna is income-tested: earnings above the threshold can reduce the benefit or cancel it (from 70 it is paid regardless of earnings). The app does not calculate the benefit — check your threshold: <a href=\"https://www.kolzchut.org.il/he/%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%91%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%97_%D7%95%D7%AA%D7%99%D7%A7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kol Zchut — קצבת אזרח ותיק</a>.",
"ret.check70":"From age 70 kitzbat zikna is paid regardless of earnings. If you are 70+ and not receiving it — check your entitlement with Bituach Leumi; meanwhile the calculation uses the reduced no-kitzba rates.",
"rep.body":"<div class=\"b-row\"><span class=\"n\">January</span><span class=\"v\">form 101 — every employee, at the employer</span></div><div class=\"b-row\"><span class=\"n\">Start of year</span><span class=\"v\">osek patur turnover declaration (check your VAT notice)</span></div><div class=\"b-row\"><span class=\"n\">15th monthly</span><span class=\"v\">VAT (murshe), advances, self-employed NI</span></div><div class=\"b-row\"><span class=\"n\">By March 31</span><span class=\"v\">form 106 from the employer for last year</span></div><div class=\"b-row\"><span class=\"n\">By May 31</span><span class=\"v\">annual return of the self-employed</span></div><div class=\"b-row\"><span class=\"n\">All year</span><span class=\"v\">tax refund — can be filed for 6 past years</span></div>",
