"lt.x.tlush":"Translation: “Dear employer, under the Wage Protection Law a payslip must be given to the employee by the 9th. Please provide my payslips for: {month}. Thank you for handling this promptly. Respectfully, {name}”",
"lt.x.pay":"Translation: “Dear employer, per my personal record I worked {hours} hours in {month}. By my calculation the salary paid does not match the hours worked (approx. gap: {diff} ₪). Please check the calculation and pay the difference with the next salary, per the Wage Protection Law and the Minimum Wage Law. I would appreciate a full hours breakdown in the payslip. Respectfully, {name}”",
"lt.x.pension":"Translation: “Dear employer, please provide confirmation of deposits (ishur afkadot) to my pension fund for recent months, per the mandatory-pension extension order. If there are gaps between payslip deductions and actual deposits — please settle them. Respectfully, {name}”",
"lt.x.delay":"Translation: “Dear employer, the salary for {month} has not yet been paid. Under the Wage Protection Law wages are due by the 9th; past that date this is halanat sachar entitling compensation. Please pay immediately. Respectfully, {name}”",
"lt.x.worse":"Notice of worsened conditions (haraat tnaim) under sec. 11(a): you give the employer 14 days to fix it. If they do not, resigning may be treated as dismissal with severance rights retained.",
"lt.x.warn":"Michtav hatraa — a formal warning before going to the labour court: you list the violation and give 7 days to fix it. Such a letter often settles the matter and serves as evidence in court.",
"lt.x.havraa":"Reminder about unpaid havra’a: due after a full year of tenure, the number of days grows with seniority, and the rate depends on the sector (private ₪418; public, cleaning and security ₪511.60).",
"lt.x.miluim":"Notice of a reserve-duty call-up with a copy attached. During the service and 30 days after it dismissal is prohibited without a committee permit; the pay is compensated by National Insurance.",
"lt.x.vacation":"Annual vacation request: dates and number of days from your accrued balance. Dates are coordinated with the employer, but the right to vacation is statutory.",
"lt.x.hours":"Request to clarify the payslip: breakdown of hours and overtime, vacation and sick-day balances, correction of an error in the next payslip.",
"lt.x.t106":"Request for the annual Form 106 — yearly income and withheld tax. Without it you cannot check a tax refund (claimable up to 6 years back). The employer must issue it by 31 March.",
"lt.x.ishur":"Request for an employment certificate (ishur haasaka): period, position, scope. Needed for National Insurance, banks and the Tax Authority; it must be issued within 14 days of termination.",
"lt.x.resign":"Resignation notice: you give the statutory advance notice (hodaa mukdemet), state your last working day and ask for the final settlement (vacation payout, havra’a), an employment certificate and the pension-fund release letter.",
