"hol.rules":"<b>Working on a holiday</b> — at least 150% plus a substitute rest day.<br><b>Dmei chag (דמי חגים) — pay for a non-working holiday.</b> Hourly and daily-paid workers get it after 3 months of tenure: the holiday is paid like a regular working day, provided you did not skip the day before or after without permission. Monthly-salaried workers simply keep their full salary — there is no separate payslip line for them.<br>A holiday falling on Shabbat is not paid separately if Saturday is a non-working day for you anyway.",
