"ind.help":"<b>Sector minimum rates (2026, verified):</b><br>General — ₪35.40/hour (₪6,443.85/month).<br>Cleaning — ₪39.11/hour by the extension order (supervisor 39.16) + pension from day 1, hishtalmut, public-rate havra’a.<br>Security — ₪39.11/hour + hishtalmut from day 1, shai la-chag.<br>Construction — by grade: grade 3 from ₪6,900/month, grade 4 from ₪7,600, site manager from ₪10,000; pension from day 1.<br>Catering — ₪35.40/hour; institutional catering (factory/hospital canteens) — at least 113% of the general minimum (≈₪40/hour).<br>Caregiving — no sector order, the general minimum ₪35.40/hour applies.<br>The chosen sector feeds the correct minimum into the overtime rate and the payslip check.","prof.tenure":"Tenure, years",
"prof.tenure.hint":"This tenure does not change the net. It is used in three places: the construction hishtalmut gate (3 years of sector tenure), auto-fill of the dismissal calculator (severance, notice, havra’a) and the sector payslip check (day-1 pension, the havra’a days ladder).","prof.extra":"Other grounds (degree, alimony, discharge) — points","prof.hish":"I have keren hishtalmut (7.5% / 2.5%)",
 "brk.hish":"Keren hishtalmut (2.5%)","employer.hish":"Employer keren hishtalmut (7.5%)","ot.add":"➕ Add to gross in the calculator",
 "ai.t.morepoints":"<b>What it is.</b> Nekudot zikuy (נקודות זיכוי) — tax credit points that reduce the tax itself. <b>Each point = ₪242/month</b> (₪2,904/year). Tax never goes below zero: unused points are not paid out.<br><b>Base</b> (residents, olim and A/5 visa holders): man + 2.25 · woman + 2.75.<br><b>Per child</b> (age in the tax year):<br>• under 1: +2.5 mother, +2.5 father<br>• 1–2 years: +4.5 mother, +4.5 father<br>• 3 years: +3.5 mother, +3.5 father<br>• 4–5 years: +2.5 mother, +2.5 father<br>• 6–17 years: +2 mother, +1 father<br>• the year the child turns 18: +0.5 mother, 0 father<br><b>Child with a disability</b> +2 points to one parent by choice (parents living apart — both).<br><b>Oleh chadash</b> (עולה חדש) has 54 benefit months from the aliyah date:<br>• months 1–12: +1 point<br>• months 13–30: +3 points<br>• months 31–42: +2 points<br>• months 43–54: +1 point<br>IDF service and full-time studies pause the counter.<br><b>For studies</b> (from the year following graduation):<br>• BA + 1 point — 2023+ graduates for the number of study years, max 3; 2014–2022 graduates — for 1 year<br>• MA + 0.5 point (2023+ — for 2 years)<br>• State professional diploma of 1,700+ hours + 1 point (study period, max 3 years)<br>BA and the professional diploma do not add up — you pick one; MA combines with either.<br><b>Other:</b> discharged soldiers + 2 points (full service) / +1 (partial), valid 36 months after discharge · alimony to an ex-spouse +1 · non-working spouse (retirement age or disability) +1 · single parent +1 · residents of peripheral towns — a 7–20% tax discount per the official list.<br>Claimed at hiring: Form 101 (טופס 101) + supporting certificates. Overpaid tax can be refunded up to 6 years back.",
 "prof.ind.general":"General","prof.ind.cleaning":"Cleaning","prof.ind.security":"Security","prof.ind.construction":"Construction","prof.ind.catering":"Catering","prof.ind.care":"Caregiving",
 "prof.hish.hint":"<b>What it is:</b> keren hishtalmut (קרן השתלמות) — your personal tax-advantaged savings fund, a «second pension».<br><b>How it fills up:</b> 2.5% from your salary + 7.5% added by the employer = 10% a month into your account.<br><b>When to withdraw:</b> after 6 years — the whole amount, tax-free.<br><b>Who must get it (extension orders):</b><br>• cleaning and security — from day one;<br>• construction — site workers after <b>3 years of seniority in the industry</b> (in Israel, across all employers); foremen and crane operators — from day 1. Office staff of construction firms (accounting, HR, marketing) are NOT covered by the construction order;<br>• <b>foreign construction workers (B1/2a5) don't get a fund opened</b> — instead, after 3 years of industry seniority they're owed a cash supplement «chalaf hishtalmut» (חלף השתלמות). No supplement — underpayment;<br>• manpower-agency workers may fall under a different agreement.<br>In other industries — only if your contract says so.<br><b>Simple rule:</b> the השתלמות line exists in your payslip → tick the box; no line → untick (and if the list above entitles you — demand it in writing).<br><b>Nuance:</b> percentages apply to the base salary — overtime and one-off bonuses aren't included (the app calculates it that way).",
 "fired.h":"Dismissal calculator: what am I owed","fired.hint":"A legal-minimum estimate for dismissal by the employer (or equivalent resignation). Fill in — see the full settlement.",
 "fired.paytype":"Pay type","fired.monthly":"Monthly","fired.hourlyp":"Hourly",
 "fired.gross":"Last gross, ₪/month","fired.tenure":"Tenure, years","fired.vacdays":"Unused vacation days","fired.havdays":"Unpaid havra’a days (דמי הבראה)",
 "fired.res.pitz":"Pitzuim (פיצויי פיטורים) — severance pay","fired.res.notice":"Hodaa mukdemet (הודעה מוקדמת) — notice pay, days:","fired.res.vac":"Pidyon chufsha (פדיון חופשה) — unused vacation payout","fired.res.hav":"Havra’a (דמי הבראה) — recuperation pay",
"fired.hav.pub":"public sector / cleaning / security",
"fired.hav.priv":"private sector",
"fired.hav.rate":"₪{r}/day, {s}","fired.total":"Total settlement",
 "fired.note":"<b>How to read this estimate:</b><br>• <b>Pitzuim (פיצויי פיטורים — severance pay):</b> one monthly gross salary per year worked; due after a full year of tenure.<br>• <b>Check the «Section 14» clause (סעיף 14) in your contract.</b> Most contracts have it, and it means: the employer has already been depositing your severance monthly — 8.33% of salary — into your pension fund. In that case you collect that money FROM THE FUND (call them and ask for the severance component), not from the employer. If only 6% was deposited — the employer tops up the difference himself.<br>• <b>Pidyon chufsha (פדיון חופשה — payout of unused vacation):</b> a vacation day = gross ÷ 21.67 (5-day week).<br>• <b>Havraa (דמי הבראה — annual recreation pay, due after one year):</b> calculated at your sector's daily rate: cleaning/security/public — 511.60 ₪, private — 418 ₪.<br>• All of this is the legal minimum; sectors with a tzav harchava (צו הרחבה — an extension order applying a collective agreement to the whole sector) may owe you more.<br>• An employment-period certificate must be issued within 14 days of dismissal.<br>⚠️ <b>Court deadlines:</b> a claim for unpaid vacation — up to 3 years from dismissal; claims for unpaid wages and severance — up to 7 years.<br>• <b>Shimua (שימוע — pre-dismissal hearing):</b> the employer must invite you in writing in advance, state the reasons and let you respond; the decision is not announced on the spot. Dismissal without a hearing, or with a sham one, is compensated separately by the court — in practice 1 to 6–12 monthly salaries on top of severance.<br>• <b>Unused sick days are NOT paid out</b> on termination — in the private sector they simply expire (a payout exists in the public sector and under some collective agreements — check yours).<br>• <b>Tax on severance:</b> exempt up to ₪12,640 per year of work (2026). Anything above that is taxed at your marginal rate; for large amounts consider «retzef pitzuim» (רצף פיצויים — rolling it into the fund) instead of taking cash.",
 "emp.ot.exp":"➕ This month's overtime (125% / 150%)","emp.ot.hint":"The hourly rate is taken automatically: gross ÷ 182. The overtime pay joins the taxable gross — income tax and National Insurance are computed on the full amount, while pension and hishtalmut, as the law requires, are computed on the base salary only.",
